ay  say I I I think we got our nap we got  this we cracked it like when did you  start to look at each other and go all  right don't worry we've got our movie  here it is  well I I don't think obviously you never  reached that point where you think we've  got it's always a work in progress  everything is always a work in progress  but but I remember speaking to Dave and  saying Dave that there are some there's  going to be a lot of ideas in there that  we've discussed that we're not sure  about so we're going to leave them in  because because we're not sure we could  things could change things could move  around and so I think we ended up  sending a lot more ideas than than you  know just as a sort of a backup really  to give you some maneuverability but  actually I think quite a lot of the  ideas just stayed in and all played  together didn't they in many of the  scenes they really did we uh because  Brett and I went and worked together  well Paul was off working on the music  um Brett and I went through and just  spent days and days going through  effects and what would work here against  a guy track of music that we had  and uh so yeah I think  everything yeah kind of in there yeah  it's all over and and I think one of the  other things that we that we talked  about a lot as well was was how to  um sort of bring to life a lot of those  kind of concerts and the concert crowds  and and who are  um if you want to speak about yeah I  mean obviously all those performances it  was so crucial to try and make the  audience feel like they were  experiencing Bowie in those moments and  meeting him the first time and  transported in time if you like to Ziggy  Stardust walking on stage and so we did  an awful lot of listening through we had  such a fantastic library of material  there of all of his performances and how  the crowds responded to him at different  times throughout his career and we  really Drew on that in creating the  crowds to make sure that we were being  au